  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 151 PM CDT Sun May 10 2026\n\nA dry and stable pattern will prevail for most of next week.\nAn upper level ridge over the southwestern U.S. will migrate \neastward into our area by the middle of the week. The center of \nthe ridge axis will shift to the east of the region on Thursday \nand Friday with generally zonal flow aloft prevailing into next \nweekend. Next weekend models forecast an upper level low to deepen\nover southern California and the Baja. With embedded disturbances\nin the southwest flow and the dryline in play may see scattered \nthunderstorm development on Sunday. For now will keep PoPs capped \nat 20-30 percent but will need to watch. Otherwise, temperatures \nwill warm into the upper 80s to mid 90s across most of the area \nfrom Wednesday into next weekend, with some upper 90s and triple \ndigits possible in the Big County on Friday and Saturday.",
